# oracle-tolerance: pe agrees to 1e-12 relative; the pressure (about 0.002 bar-units in metal units, a near-zero stress at the ideal state) agrees to 3e-9 absolute, which the rel 1e-7 abs 1e-7 window covers
# oracle: pair_style meam, 108-atom periodic hcp Ti crystal (4-atom orthorhombic cell, 3x3x3 cells, a1 = a, a2 = sqrt3 a, a3 = c, hcp basis) with nn2(1,1) = 1, parameters w47mn_ti.meam (Ti of FeTiClibrary.meam), five states (a, c/a): ideal c/a at 2.92, 2.70 and 3.10 A, and c/a 1.55 and 1.70 at 2.92 and 2.80 A
# oracle: the 6 second-neighbour atoms at sqrt2 a and the reference structure of the hcp 2NN recurrence; the native energies are the black-box values in this file
# oracle-potentials: FeTiClibrary.meam
# oracle-inputs: w47mn_ti.meam
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-7 abs=1e-7
clear
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p p
lattice         custom 1.0 a1 2.920000000000 0 0 a2 0 5.057588358101 0 a3 0 0 4.768340032618 &
                basis 0 0 0 basis 0.5 0.5 0 basis 0 0.333333333333333333 0.5 basis 0.5 0.833333333333333333 0.5
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 47.88
pair_style      meam
pair_coeff      * * FeTiClibrary.meam Ti w47mn_ti.meam Ti
thermo_style    custom step pe press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             0
